We promised it long ago

41
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,940
They're gonna duel!

42
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,730
Huh?

43
00:02:33,813 --> 00:02:34,643
Who's going to?

44
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:38,980
Lord Judge has taken on
that pirate Sanji Sanji?

45
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:43,860
And I heard he already beat up Master
Yoji What kind of monster is he?

46
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:55,721
That lout was still refusing the marriage,
so I tried to step in on Father's behalf.

47
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:57,380
Just like old times.

48
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,280
And then this happens!

49
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,180
He'll pay for this!

50
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,120
He's such an arrogant asshole!

51
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:07,536
It appears we'll need to use a tool
more powerful than the hammer, sir.

52
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,119
Starting to press.

53
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,180
Hold still a second. Huh?

54
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,800
And I believe that does it.

55
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,140
Screw that guy.

56
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:31,420
He's a reject, a
disappointment, and a failure.

57
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,360
That's Master Sanji.

58
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,640
I trust you're prepared.

59
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,020
Anytime you're ready.

60
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:48,620
Very well.

61
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:51,780
Time to duel!

62
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,980
They're both so quick.

63
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,340
It's no surprise.

64
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:16,696
Master Sanji had a hefty
bounty on his head after all.

65
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,071
It's not a shame to kick your father, huh?

66
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,117
Guess the guy who started
this in the first place.

67
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,400
And stop saying you're my father.

68
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,129
It's getting on my nerves.

69
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:45,540
Like it or not, you are my son, Saji.

70
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:48,560
So why are you trying to stab me then?

71
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:49,777
He's powerful.

72
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:52,389
And he's fighting
without a raid suit, too.

73
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:57,514
Once the tea party ends, I'm
booking it back to my ship.

74
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,940
I won't really marry her.

75
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,780
Still spouting off.

76
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:08,957
This is all about strengthening your forces
by forming a bond with Big Mom, right?

77
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,687
So it shouldn't matter
where I go afterwards.

78
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:14,380
The issue is not that simple.

79
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,460
You'd stain the Vinsmoke name.

80
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,739
Big Mom would punish such treasury.

81
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:23,757
You'd be mistaken if you think I give
a crap what happens to you chumps.

82
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:27,300
Besides, I only came here
to save my friends' lives.

83
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,120
You depended your family?

84
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:33,660
You bastards were never my family!

85
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,240
Yep, he was in the kitchen.

86
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:43,307
Sanji was making some
of that rat food again.

87
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,420
Royalty doesn't cook.

88
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:50,580
You shut up!

89
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:51,580
Give it back!

90
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,110
Ouch.

91
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:00,460
You piece of trash!

92
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,189
Don't ever touch me again!

93
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,720
Oh, it is so weak!

94
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:09,257
You were all bored all the same day!

95
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,560
How are we related to such a loser?

96
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:24,300
You're a failure.

97
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,520
Father's here.

98
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:43,180
Picking on Sanji again?

99
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,320
They hurt me, Father.

100
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,100
Can you tell them to stop?

101
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,540
Why should I?

102
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,170
Father...

103
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:04,397
If you are not a fighter and you
are unable to stand up for yourself,

104
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,820
I have no obligation to help you.

105
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,960
I gain nothing by raising you.

106
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,380
Why would you say that?

107
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:19,760
You're a disgrace to the family name.

108
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:32,060
On your feet, I'll toughen you up!

109
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:36,180
You're such a disgrace?

110
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:39,340
All right, Yonji have at him.

111
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,220
This is gonna be fun

112
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:48,730
Ha!

113
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,920
Reminiscing on old times, are you?

114
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,940
He blocked the blade with his leg.

115
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,660
The evil son I once knew
we'll talk, you know?

116
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:27,480
Fetch a sword. Huh? Sir!

117
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:32,300
Take it.

118
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:36,280
What's the matter?

119
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:39,031
Surely you haven't forgotten my teachings.

120
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:48,260
If you knew me at all, you'd
realize I never use that crap.

121
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,740
Get this through your skull.

122
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,880
My hands are for cooking only.

123
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:38,520
Wow, weak little Sanji's
become quite strong.

124
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:40,200
For cooking, you say?

125
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,820
That's absurd.

126
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:44,120
Are you still making rat food?

127
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:47,220
Serving is not a talent befit for royalty.

128
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:48,500
It's ludicrous.

129
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:51,160
You're out of touch, old man.

130
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,840
Why resist the marriage?

131
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,119
Don't you know what's good for you?

132
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:13,902
He's still in close combat mode.

133
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,780
So this is how the
legendary Carrot fights.

134
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:18,857
You don't get to see this every day.

135
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:20,220
An aerial attack?

136
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,660
How ironic.

137
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:22,921
That's my forte.

138
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,520
Diablo-jamba.

139
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,600
Gol-yay. Go!

140
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:30,890
Go!

141
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:47,360
War is the catalyst for
scientific progress!

142
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:51,860
Electromagnetic crux!

143
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,340
Blaster!

144
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:19,220
The Germa you were once familiar
with is now a relic of the past.

145
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:50,060
Little Sanji, I got
something I want to ask.

146
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,746
Do you owe someone respect just
because you're elated by blood?

147
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,040
What do you say?

148
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:07,160
Any fond memories of him?

149
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,820
Can't think of one, can you?

150
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,920
I'm sorry.

151
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:21,200
Father, let me out!

152
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,760
You suffered so much.

153
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:35,857
It's so dark in here!

154
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,240
Please, Father!

155
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,580
Boil up, Freer!

156
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,820
I'm sure you've got nothing
but anger towards him.

157
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:52,980
Wall up!

158
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:58,580
Look out!

159
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,525
He's heading straight for you!

160
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,760
E .M.

161
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,120
Chef, go!

162
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:52,500
I'm surprised.

163
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:54,234
You're tough as nails.

164
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:00,580
I still can't believe
you're the same Sanji.

165
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:02,660
You are so helpless.

166
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,080
You can save the small talk.

167
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,317
After this damn tea party's over, I'm out.

168
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:11,357
Then I'll be free from Big
Mom's invitation curse.

169
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:16,087
I was hoping you'd be less of a scumbag,
but it seems you've only gotten worse.

170
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,926
Get out of this room, geezer.

171
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,520
You're stranger to me.

172
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:21,040
No chance.

173
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:24,560
Need I remind you that's
my blood in your veins?

174
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,620
Do not be mistaken.

175
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,780
What you witnessed today, boy?,

176
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,040
was an example of how loyal
the Germa soldiers truly are?

177
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:36,142
willing to give their
lives at a moment's notice.

178
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:40,620
Their unwavering devotion is
the backbone of Jerma's power.

179
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:47,687
Then why the hell aren't you using them
to chase your stupid, grandiose dreams?

180
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,537
You wanted to conquer
the North Blue, right?

181
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:51,450
Terrific.

182
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:53,640
That's perfect for an evil army.

183
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,450
Precisely.

184
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:57,168
You're quick on the uptake.

185
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:02,280
By forming an alliance with Big Mom,
it will strengthen our forces tenfold.

186
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:05,300
And that dream can soon become a reality.

187
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:12,200
If you can comprehend at least
that much, I'm satisfied.

188
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:18,060
Honestly, I did not intend to
ruffle any feathers, Sanji.

189
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,560
I require Big Mom's help,

190
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:27,191
but unfortunately she demands
a blood connection in return.

191
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:28,350
Frankly,

192
00:15:28,433 --> 00:15:30,997
I do not relish the thought
of marrying off one of my

193
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:34,786
invaluable sons to someone in
that demented madwoman's lineage.

194
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:40,960
Then I remembered, years
ago, I had another child.

195
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,700
Who was an absolute failure?

196
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:48,100
You'll be a sacrifice for
the family, understood?

197
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:54,460
I haven't changed my opinion of you, and
I do not think of you as a worthy son.

198
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,060
Just so we're clear.

199
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:02,010
Huh?

200
00:16:02,093 --> 00:16:03,180
What's this about?

201
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:06,186
You mentioned your hands
are important to you.

202
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:07,760
That works in my favor.

203
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:12,620
You know of the collars the Celestial
Dragons put on their slaves, yes?

204
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:17,940
If they try to escape from their masters,
it detonates, removing their heads.

205
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,220
These are rigged to work the same way.

206
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:24,500
If you try to flee, your
hands will be blown off.

207
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,440
Huh? Screw you! Take them off!

208
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:31,357
Fortunately, Big Mom had the
foresight to lend those to me.

209
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:33,852
She's the only one who possesses the key.

210
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:34,920
Are you serious?

211
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,080
Stop that.

212
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,860
I wouldn't fuss with them if I were you.

213
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:50,885
Using the key is the only
way to take them off.

214
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:52,240
Safely, that is.

215
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,960
You can't run away.

216
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,600
Cuffs or no cuffs.

217
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:04,620
Because I have the entire German
army to put you in your place.

218
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,960
We will see this marriage through.

219
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:17,530
Extra!

220
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,140
Soto Land News!

221
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:22,140
I can't believe Boss
Jinbei betrayed Big Mom.

222
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:24,197
It says it all happened yesterday.

223
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:25,280
Things move fast.

224
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,060
That's a crying shame.

225
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:32,617
The way he marched on up and stopped
Mama's food tantrum was pretty damn cool.

226
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:35,437
Well, as I understand it,
he has to leave her crew.

227
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:39,577
You better believe he took that back in
a second soon as he heard the price wait.

228
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:40,490
Are you for real?

229
00:17:40,573 --> 00:17:41,716
Wow, that's pathetic

230
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:49,277
I guess being the first son of the sea
means nothing to that traitor, man.

231
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,440
I lost respect for that coward.

232
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:52,540
What a loser

233
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:56,770
I

234
00:17:57,740 --> 00:18:01,577
was unaware you were working
for big mom that must

235
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:04,484
be why fish man island
was under her protection?

236
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:10,300
So this Jinbei fellow, he was
a former warlord, that correct?

237
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,134
How's someone like him her subordinate?

238
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:17,200
Tell me, Brook, do you
Karoo know this man? We do.

239
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:19,836
He's a rather important person to us.

240
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,837
And if you haven't changed
your mind and still

241
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:25,508
wish for me to become
a member of your crew,

242
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:30,240
well, I'll gladly take you up on your
offer then, if you see fit to have me.

243
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:34,836
I suppose this is what he
meant by having obligations.

244
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:39,682
I wonder what kind of business he
could have with Big Mom, though.

245
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,722
This article still befuddles me.

246
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,632
It doesn't sound like the Jinbei we know.

247
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,980
Is he preparing to come see us?

248
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,600
Hey, Brooke!

249
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:52,980
Can we hurry?

250
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:55,085
I have somewhere I need to go.

251
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,677
Mademoiselle Pudding, whatever
your matter of urgency is,

252
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:58,777
it can wait, n 'est-ce pas?

253
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:02,377
Nothing could be more important
than choosing the correct author!

254
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:03,400
I'll be late.

255
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,040
Lady Pudding!

256
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,347
What's your opinion on this?

257
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:09,444
I think it would suit you well.

258
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:11,820
How about this one? I knew it.

259
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,077
That color will look wonderful on you.

260
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,017
